# promise: #522
# Information about a tab from another space came up when the pointer rested in the middle of the
# page, in full screen with the sidebar shown, once the window was back on its first space (#522). The
# spaces sit side by side on a strip beside the sidebar: on a 1440-point window the third space's list
# and tiles lie two sidebar widths in, under the middle of the page, and their tracking areas reached
# over it, as the next space's did for #527 (sidebar-hover-other-space, sidebar-tip-other-space). Only
# the space shown takes the pointer, wherever on the strip the others are, after a switch away and back.
